    "lesson": {
      "title": "Heat through a spoon",
      "instruction": "Why does heat reach a metal handle sooner than a wooden one?",
      "explanation": "Uniform one-dimensional cell-centred rod: alpha=k/(rho*cp). Bath held constant at one end; far end and sides insulated. Explicit finite-volume fluxes with Fourier number≤.2; reject over200000 steps. Comparison holds rho*cp and geometry equal to isolate conductivity1/100W/m/K; teaching approximations, not actual utensil property presets. No side heat losses."
